<div class="split">
  <div class="prose">
    <p class="lead">Whether you traveled from across the country or just across the city, your presence made the 80th Anniversary truly special.</p>

    <h2>Friday, April 10 — Alumni Reunion Banquet</h2>
    <p>The evening brought together alumni spanning decades of 395 Squadron history for an unforgettable night at the Chateau Louis Conference Centre.</p>
    <p>Over cocktails, dinner, and great conversation, old friendships were rekindled and new ones were made.</p>
    <p>We were honoured to hear from our guest speaker, Major Andrew Brown, Commanding Officer of 417 Squadron at CFB Cold Lake, whose words reminded us all of the enduring value of the Air Cadet program.</p>
    <p>A presentation tracing the history of 395 Squadron drew plenty of smiles, laughs, and more than a few proud memories.</p>

    <h2>Saturday, April 11 — Commemorative Parade</h2>
    <p>The weekend continued at the Jefferson Armouries, where alumni gathered alongside current cadets for a commemorative parade marking 80 years of service to Edmonton’s youth. It was a powerful reminder that the legacy we share is very much alive and in good hands.</p>
